1
00:00:13,660 --> 00:00:14,490
All right!

2
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:17,637
I finally obtained the disc
that contains Star Platinum!

3
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:18,860
Jolene Kujo,

4
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:24,124
is it possible she defeated that incumbent
guard and took the disc all by herself?

5
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:32,000
I'm gonna get my dad's
disc out of this prison,

6
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:35,380
and that includes the one
Palesnake's holding on to.

7
00:00:36,220 --> 00:00:37,050
Just watch.

8
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:39,440
Of course,

9
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:44,780
I erased all knowledge of myself from
Mirachan's memory disc, an obvious choice.

10
00:00:45,480 --> 00:00:48,117
And therefore, nobody can reach me.

11
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:52,417
The true difference between a
human and an animal is nothing less

12
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:56,206
than whether or not they desire
to go to heaven after they die.

13
00:00:56,360 --> 00:01:00,377
People should live their lives in such a
manner that they'll be led into heaven.

14
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:04,620
For that is the beauty inherent
in the nature of humankind.

15
00:01:43,880 --> 00:01:48,100
I don't want to say it!

16
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,120
Let's go!

17
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:53,240
1, 2, 3 Come and find a way!

18
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:03,280
Break out without me, you

19
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,797
I'm going to use the phone now, right?

20
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:49,710
Ah?

21
00:02:49,793 --> 00:02:50,960
Are you insane, girl?

22
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:53,747
Get that gun out of my
face or I'll beat you.

23
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:58,300
Oh, my mistake.

24
00:02:58,580 --> 00:03:01,227
Please sit down so your
feet don't get tired.

25
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:05,980
By the way, here's a
cold can of cola for you.

26
00:03:06,220 --> 00:03:07,197
Enjoy your drink.

27
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:08,456
Come again any time.

28
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:23,805
This is the Speedwagon Foundation
headquarters in Dallas, Texas.

29
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:27,817
Please be advised, we don't
accept collect calls on this line.

30
00:03:27,900 --> 00:03:29,537
But I looked in the phone book.

31
00:03:29,620 --> 00:03:31,091
This is all I could find.

32
00:03:31,660 --> 00:03:33,248
Just listen for one second.

33
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:36,717
I'm an inmate incarcerated at the
Green Dolphin Street prison in Florida.

34
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:38,780
And my name is Jolene Cujo.

35
00:03:39,120 --> 00:03:42,414
Please connect me to somebody
who knows what that means.

36
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:43,940
Please hold.

37
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,897
Sorry for the wait.

38
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:54,900
Are you the daughter of Professor
Jotaro Kujo? And you are?

39
00:03:55,940 --> 00:03:57,957
I'm just a Foundation representative.

40
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:00,720
Also, so you know, I'm not a stand user.

41
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:03,150
Oh.

42
00:04:03,233 --> 00:04:05,017
Still, you clearly know
about stands, though.

43
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:07,629
Do you happen to know
anything about discs?

44
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:09,097
Yes, of course.

45
00:04:09,180 --> 00:04:10,040
After Dr.

46
00:04:10,180 --> 00:04:15,121
Jotaro Kujo's body was retrieved from the
UUV, he wasn't transferred here to Dallas.

47
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:20,357
Nevertheless, rest assured, his body
is being sheltered in a safe area.

48
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:23,580
However, it's really rather
unfortunate, you see.

49
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:28,240
But there are, well, no signs
of life, medically speaking.

50
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:31,050
Shit.

51
00:04:31,133 --> 00:04:33,526
Would you believe me
that he could be revived?

52
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:35,360
I'm merely a scientist.

53
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:36,917
I can't...

54
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:39,820
I've obtained one disc. I have it.

55
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:41,472
He'll come back to life.

56
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:45,425
I'm certain that my father will
definitely regenerate with this.

57
00:04:45,740 --> 00:04:49,417
I want to give the Foundation
this disc by any means necessary,

58
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:50,735
but I don't know how.

59
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:53,201
You need to come up with an idea.

60
00:04:53,340 --> 00:04:55,737
I want to get the disc out of this prison.

61
00:04:55,820 --> 00:04:56,650
Immediately.

62
00:04:57,620 --> 00:05:01,502
Excuse me, miss, but isn't this
call being recorded by the prison?

63
00:05:01,660 --> 00:05:03,180
Yes, it probably is.

64
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:06,037
Trust me, I'm fully aware
of that possibility.

65
00:05:06,120 --> 00:05:07,540
But I have no time, sir.

66
00:05:07,780 --> 00:05:08,777
It's extremely urgent.

67
00:05:08,860 --> 00:05:09,919
It's now or never.

68
00:05:10,140 --> 00:05:12,237
I'm in an unbelievably
dangerous situation.

69
00:05:12,320 --> 00:05:14,555
I can't safely hide the disc anywhere.

70
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:18,293
There's gotta be a way for this to work.

71
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:21,557
Just so you know, though, I'm
not allowed to have any visitors.

72
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:22,470
I understand.

73
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:23,740
If you insist.

74
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:27,354
Meet in the courtyard.

75
00:05:27,640 --> 00:05:28,640
In the courtyard?

76
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:32,937
You talking about the one sandwiched
between the women's and men's prisons?

77
00:05:33,020 --> 00:05:34,297
Exactly, that's the one.

78
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:38,086
If you can meet us there in 20
minutes, I think I have an idea.

79
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:39,590
Wait.

80
00:05:39,673 --> 00:05:40,520
Get there in 20 minutes?

81
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:41,920
From right now?

82
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:43,430
Yes.

83
00:05:43,513 --> 00:05:44,554
It's urgent, isn't it?

84
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:49,057
If you want us to collect the disk,
we will do so with the utmost effort.

85
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:52,022
If you say he'll be revived,
then we believe you.

86
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:53,550
However,

87
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:57,657
you must understand that we are an
unarmed chemotherapy research association.

88
00:05:57,740 --> 00:05:58,680
As a result,

89
00:05:59,060 --> 00:06:01,237
the Speedwagon Foundation
cannot help you escape

90
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,967
from the prison or
protect you from any harm.

91
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:07,197
Still willing to take the risk
and come to the courtyard?

92
00:06:07,280 --> 00:06:08,940
Yes. I'll go.

93
00:06:10,040 --> 00:06:12,377
So, how exactly do I get it to you?

94
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:15,284
We shouldn't discuss that
matter over the phone.

95
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:18,940
All I can say is, please
look for Savage Guardian.

96
00:06:19,280 --> 00:06:20,633
It'll make sense there.

97
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:25,420
How about we call this
Operation Savage Guardian?

98
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:30,940
Savage Guardian?

99
00:06:31,340 --> 00:06:32,520
Is that a thing?

100
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:33,800
Or a person?

101
00:06:34,980 --> 00:06:35,810
Whatever.

102
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:37,017
I'll figure it out.

103
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:38,837
I gotta head to the courtyard.

104
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:40,537
From Floor One's cafeteria.

105
00:06:40,620 --> 00:06:42,860
In order to get to the courtyard,

106
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:47,279
first I have to go through that
gate, then walk upstairs in the back,

107
00:06:47,380 --> 00:06:50,057
and finally, cross over
the connecting corridor

108
00:06:50,140 --> 00:06:52,237
on the second floor into the medical wing.

109
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:54,300
You may go through. Huh?

110
00:06:54,640 --> 00:06:56,880
You're FE40536.

111
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:59,937
You're the nuisance who was
sent to the punishment cell.

112
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:03,237
You're restricted from accessing
certain parts of the prison.

113
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,150
Huh?

114
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:15,430
Jolene!

115
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:17,160
Emporio! Here!

116
00:07:17,420 --> 00:07:18,891
Don't touch the baseball!

117
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:25,630
Huh?

118
00:07:25,713 --> 00:07:28,540
I can't let anyone see me. Come on.

119
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:47,980
Hey, Emporio, who are those guys?

120
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:50,596
Oh, don't worry, they're not enemies.

121
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,677
He'd prefer to sleep in a bed, of
course, but unfortunately for him,

122
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:55,737
there simply isn't one
to be found in this room.

123
00:07:55,820 --> 00:07:59,996
So naturally, he's got no other choice
but to sleep in the grand piano.

124
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:10,277
Jolene, this spot is the
ghost room I call home.

125
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:11,977
It's the place where I live.

126
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:13,100
A ghost room?

127
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:15,520
Wait, are you a ghost?

128
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:17,060
Of course not, Jolene.

129
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:18,957
Neither of us are ghosts.

130
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:20,897
We're both actual living humans.

131
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:22,257
Go ahead and touch me.

132
00:08:22,340 --> 00:08:24,297
I have a body temperature and a pulse.

133
00:08:24,380 --> 00:08:25,420
Listen carefully.

134
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:28,624
It's not like this room
is inhabited by a ghost.

135
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:30,480
Rather, the room is a ghost.

136
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:33,010
Huh?

137
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:35,837
Would you understand if I
say they're ghost objects?

138
00:08:35,920 --> 00:08:38,177
The Green Dolphin Street
Prison caught fire

139
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:40,920
in 1984 and then underwent
a huge renovation.

140
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:44,897
This room was one part of the
prison which completely burned down.

141
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:49,260
We're inside objects of the past,
the ghost of the music room itself.

142
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:51,917
Wait, so...

143
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,457
Emporia, wouldn't this
mean that you're a...

144
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:55,617
that you are a...

145
00:08:55,700 --> 00:08:59,940
I was born like this, with the
ability to use these ghost objects.

146
00:09:01,140 --> 00:09:03,493
Interacting with them is my stand power.

147
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:06,608
Although, they're the
only things I can use.

148
00:09:07,080 --> 00:09:11,080
So, for example, even this chocolate
bar and Florida orange juice...

149
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:15,697
I can't actually eat either of them.

150
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:17,097
I can taste them, though.

151
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:18,356
They're pretty good.

152
00:09:23,500 --> 00:09:24,360
The heck?

153
00:09:24,820 --> 00:09:26,020
Don't worry, Jolene.

154
00:09:26,620 --> 00:09:30,077
That little clock got stopped
when the prison was burnt down.

155
00:09:30,160 --> 00:09:33,278
There is still time until
that meeting in 20 minutes.

156
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:34,570
However...

157
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:38,877
You're discussing how to sneak the
disc out of this prison over the phone.

158
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,431
How could you be so dumb?

159
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:43,077
I understand that you're
in a difficult situation,

160
00:09:43,160 --> 00:09:47,042
but Pale Snake is definitely going
to learn about your scheme now.

161
00:09:47,180 --> 00:09:51,237
Then please, Emporio, I need you to tell
me a shortcut to get me to the courtyard.

162
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:53,097
Hey, don't misunderstand me, Jolene.

163
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:54,897
It's not as if this
ghost room is connected

164
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:57,097
everywhere all throughout
the prison complex.

165
00:09:57,180 --> 00:10:00,097
I'm just employing the ghost items
which I can use my stand power

166
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:02,637
to interact with in order to move
around without getting caught.

167
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:03,838
Like this, you see?

168
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:06,594
Nonetheless, I know we have to do this.

169
00:10:06,980 --> 00:10:08,940
He wants to tag along with you.

170
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:12,584
It'd be a good idea to let him.

171
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:14,094
He'll be a great help.

172
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:17,700
I forgot to mention, his
name is Weather Forecast.

173
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:26,260
So this is the present-day music room?

174
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:30,801
You can let your guard
down with Weather Forecast.

175
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:34,957
The reason why he doesn't talk much
is because he lost his memories.

176
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:35,870
Memories?

177
00:10:36,780 --> 00:10:38,757
He doesn't have any
memory of his childhood,

178
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:41,487
or even how he ended up
inside of the prison.

179
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:44,217
But he has to serve a
sentence of six years.

180
00:10:44,300 --> 00:10:46,657
He likes to stretch out
and walk on his toes.

181
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:49,799
He loves reading TV guides,
but he doesn't watch TV.

182
00:10:50,020 --> 00:10:51,257
Whenever he does speak,

183
00:10:51,340 --> 00:10:52,897
he doesn't open his mouth very wide,

184
00:10:52,980 --> 00:10:55,257
so he tends to talk right
in front of your face.

185
00:10:55,340 --> 00:10:57,222
Oh, and his nose breath is warm.

186
00:10:57,880 --> 00:10:59,417
Wait, so does this mean...

187
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:03,157
Hail snake stole weather
forecast memories probably

188
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:06,097
so because of this he
wants to find out who he

189
00:11:06,180 --> 00:11:09,557
really is Also weather
forecast wants to help figure

190
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:12,758
out why your father's memory
disk was stolen from him

191
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:19,237
He said he isn't the
sort of stand user who

192
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:22,040
has been created with a
disk so it sounds like

193
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:26,340
Weather forecast was born
a stand user his power

194
00:11:29,800 --> 00:11:32,960
...is to alter and control
weather phenomenon.

195
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:35,500
It's named...

196
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:39,980
...Weather Forecast.

197
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:02,380
Just act like you didn't notice.

198
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:03,790
Pretend.

199
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:11,300
Well, seems someone was surprised by
the sound and looked inside of the room.

200
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:14,440
I was able to confirm this.

201
00:12:14,980 --> 00:12:18,537
It would appear that there's somebody
who knows you're making a move.

202
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:20,917
And they've come here to check up on you.

203
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:24,060
And now, I've seen the enemy's face.

204
00:12:29,500 --> 00:12:30,360
Oh, so cool!

205
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:45,270
Oh shit!

206
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:48,057
I had no idea he was already
this close to us all!

207
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:49,877
But if that guy is a stand user,

208
00:12:49,960 --> 00:12:52,457
then we're going to have to take
care of him right now, this instant!

209
00:12:52,540 --> 00:12:53,497
Don't do it, Jolene!

210
00:12:53,580 --> 00:12:55,286
It's better to hide from him!

211
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:56,620
Keep on running!

212
00:12:56,880 --> 00:12:59,957
He doesn't know that you're trying to
make your way over to the courtyard!

213
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:00,870
Think about it.

214
00:13:00,953 --> 00:13:04,437
He only came to find us because he must not
know what you talked about on the phone.

215
00:13:04,520 --> 00:13:08,437
If he knew what your plan was, then he
would have headed directly to the courtyard.

216
00:13:08,520 --> 00:13:13,108
That's why he's chasing after us right
now instead of trying to beat us there!

217
00:13:17,220 --> 00:13:18,597
Who the hell is that freak?

218
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:20,197
We've got to turn that corner!

219
00:13:20,280 --> 00:13:22,280
Hurry, before he catches up to us!

220
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:42,020
I was correct.

221
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:46,337
Apparently hiding was a really good idea.

222
00:13:46,420 --> 00:13:49,717
That weird man doesn't seem to have any
clue about where it is you're heading to.

223
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:52,337
But what the hell was going
on with that guy anyways?

224
00:13:52,420 --> 00:13:54,897
The way he ran on all
fours was so strange.

225
00:13:54,980 --> 00:13:56,197
We were pretty lucky.

226
00:13:56,280 --> 00:13:59,077
Good thing the dude was still
slower than us regardless.

227
00:13:59,160 --> 00:14:02,857
Still, you should make your way over to
that courtyard as soon as you possibly can.

228
00:14:02,940 --> 00:14:06,737
The phone call you made to the Speedwagon
Foundation was definitely recorded,

229
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:09,697
but I get the feeling Palesnake
hasn't actually heard that yet.

230
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:12,133
Quicker you go, less dangerous it'll be.

231
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:14,369
Medical wing's over there.

232
00:14:14,800 --> 00:14:16,917
Once you make your way
past the medical wing,

233
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:19,497
there's a gate for the
corridor around the corner.

234
00:14:19,580 --> 00:14:21,797
It leads towards the factory
and then to the men's

235
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:24,597
prison across the courtyard
you're trying to reach.

236
00:14:24,680 --> 00:14:27,637
Both the men and women prisoners
can access the medical wing.

237
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:29,877
And given that weather forecast is a guy,

238
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:32,997
if he tells the guards on duty that
he's going back to the men's prison,

239
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:35,617
then he can definitely go to the
factory entrance through the corridor.

240
00:14:35,700 --> 00:14:37,337
Or at least that's what he said to me.

241
00:14:37,420 --> 00:14:38,250
You first.

242
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:42,837
Okay, sounds like a plan, and I just
need to bribe the guards, right?

243
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:44,038
Fifty bucks enough?

244
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:47,337
Sure, but tell them that you need
to repair your boots at the factory.

245
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:48,773
No matter what, though.

246
00:14:49,060 --> 00:14:51,817
Even if you were able to go through
the medical wing of the prison,

247
00:14:51,900 --> 00:14:54,665
you'll have to get into
the courtyard by force.

248
00:14:55,220 --> 00:14:57,997
Security is light, but if you get
caught, they can shoot at you.

249
00:14:58,080 --> 00:15:01,077
You'll get yourself another
five years for prison breaking.

250
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:03,278
You think I have to force my way in?

251
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:05,796
Guess I'll just have to roll with it.

252
00:15:06,460 --> 00:15:07,840
I have no choice.

